A||N||6||kornholio||removing alternator||||9
Z||000000||kornholio||09-18-1999||12:59 AM||||Just tonight, out of the blue my car just stalled on the street and wouldn't start.  The battery was dead.  I'm pretty sure that this is a fairly new battery, so I'm guessing it's the alternator.  If I need a new alternator, I'd like to do it my self.  Is it necessary to raise the vehicle to remove the alternator? Is removing and replacing the alternator a tough task?  Thanks.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Patrick||09-18-1999||01:09 AM||||<BR>Well, you can do two things. A <B>Search</B> for "<B>alternator</B>" will turn up a ton of info. Or you can simply have a look at the thread that chronicled my adventures.<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000452.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000452.html</A> <P>Have fun!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000002||AL||09-18-1999||01:17 AM||||lift the car, get under car. you will see a bolt , take it off.next from te top or bottom you will see the top bolt take it off, remove altanator and do th reverse fr installation .it's easy just look at it and go for it, good luck||||reg||12
Z||000003||mwbackus||09-18-1999||07:21 AM||||The difficulty for r&r of an alternator differs widely and is dependent on the year, engine, and transmission type of the Fiero in question.  Older 2.8's with an automatic trans can be quite a challenge to do.  On these models, removal of the passenger wheel well liner is required, but I have heard of  methods which entail spliting the alternator while in the vehicle to ease removal.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||09-18-1999||09:08 AM||||Korny, don't be so hasty to replace the alternator. Did your charge light ever come on? If not, you could have loose or corroded wires or terminals. Clean and check everything, charge up the battery again, and run it for a while to see what happens. This happened to me once and it was only a corroded battery terminal.||||reg||1
Z||000005||kornholio||09-18-1999||05:34 PM||||Thanks guys for your quick responses.  I got the battery checked out and it was faulty, so I bought a new one and everything is fine now.  However, I don't understand why I couldn't jump start it this morning.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||09-18-1999||06:55 PM||||If a battery is totally drained or dead, jump starting won't work until you get a little bit of charge back into it. I've seen that happen more than once.||||reg||1
